00:00:03.439 --> 00:00:04.950 align:start position:0%
 
how did i get started  so i got a great question from one of my  readers dennis love you guys  dennis wrote in to me he's on my  newsletter list and i wrote in to say  evan you didn't tell me how you got  started with what you're doing man  so would you care to tell me a short  tale on that dude  dennis thanks for the question so  quick story all put together when i was  in university i had job offers from  companies that i thought would be  awesome to work with a couple years ago  and i felt like i wanted to better  myself and just try my own business  and i had a biotech software company  with two friends and  we struggled at the beginning i was  making nothing  uh and we turned it around and in a  couple years i got the company acquired  and my partners went to california as  part of the deal and i stayed here  and that's when i  i struggled to figure out what i'm going  to do next you know i'm like i'm in my  early 20s  i had the success with this company i  didn't want to go  get a job but i didn't have a burning  idea for what to do with my next company  and i've always been a big believer  that if you're not sure what you want to  do next  you don't have a burning passion for  anything yet go out and explore  try stuff and a lot of it won't work  and you get a sense of that pretty  quickly and some of it will stick and  you'll love it and opportunities will  come from that  don't try to force an idea i don't know  that's hard like that was me i'm like i  want to do something now i got to figure  this out now  you know i'd always had an interest in  venture capital i never needed it for my  business but i wanted to learn about it  so uh through a connection i ended up  with  a position at a venture capital company  in toronto helping companies raise half  a million to 15 million dollars for  companies  and i learned how the process worked and  i connected with  the three founders who were all in their  60s or 70s and had all the experience in  the world  and i had a position with them as a  associate wasn't wasn't a formal  employee relationship i could still do  whatever i wanted  but i helped bring in deals and i  learned the process because i wanted to  learn about it  i didn't think this would be a long-term  thing for me but it was something i was  curious about  at the same time i was i was in the  media a lot i was asked to speak at  events  because i was a young entrepreneur sold  the business had that success  and my first speaking gig  in toronto was at the ymca they had a  group of entrepreneurs who were  i think fired or laid off from their  jobs and they want to start their own  company as a way to  create their own path for themselves and  so  i said sure be happy to come and speak  and share my lessons and what i've  learned i'd love to help  and i spent a lot of time figuring out  everything i wanted to say and all the  things that i had learned through my  failure and then success  and i remember the day came when i was  promoting it for two weeks to my  you know friends in circles and and the  ymca was pointing it to their audience  and i spent so much time on this concept  the presentation and i was nervous you  know i wanted to be perfect  and i you know come up on that day i  remember going through the doors and my  heart's beating i'm starting to sweat  like oh my god it's coming i've been  working so hard for this moment  and i go up with this huge room ready to  go  tons of chairs and i walk into the room  open the door  and i just sink for a minute because  after all of this work three people  showed up to listen to me  i was like wow like i was promoting this  for two weeks and the ymca was pointing  it to their audience and they had a  student base already who was interested  in this  and i felt like such a failure you know  like  i spent all this time on something and  for a free event and i  can only get three people to come out  and  that was a big turning point for me  because  i could have given a crappy presentation  and  and felt like this wasn't for me and  tried something else  but what i discovered was i was there we  had three people like i'm gonna i did  all this work on the presentation so i'm  gonna make it the best presentation  these three people have ever seen  and it ended up being amazing and those  people were changed that day  and i felt the way  that i had to keep doing this it felt so  natural felt so amazing such a high  helping these people out and changing  their lives that i felt like i had to  keep going and doing this even though  anybody who looked at this would have  said evan you're crazy like  you want to turn this into a business  you this is going to be your thing now  you can't get more than three people to  come to a free event man what are you  doing this is stupid  and by all logical  reasoning it was right it was it was  stupid to think that i could turn this  into a business  and yet i loved it and so i knew i had  to find a way to keep going and if you  talk to successful entrepreneurs that's  what you'll often find is they love  what they did so much that they had to  find a way to keep going  and people would do it even if they  weren't getting paid because they loved  it so much like i  love helping entrepreneurs and i do a  lot of it without getting paid just  because it  brings me happiness and then i found a  way to turn it into  a business eventually right it wasn't i  wish i said i had this whole plan worked  out like i  sat down and i wrote my plan and this is  how it's going to work  i had i didn't have a plan you know i  was following my passion and tried to  find  something that would take me in a  direction that i would enjoy doing  and it turned from the speaking into  my website that i used to say where i  was speaking and then people  started asking could they share content  on there  i said sure you can write an article for  my website this is the time before  article marketing was anything  people wanted just to be on my site and  i use it as lead generation for  the venture capital business that i was  part of and i started talking about  modeling the masters and i started  talking about how to raise capital  put those articles up there realizing i  could sell advertising  against that and then started making  money from advertising it was a little  side thing on  just whatever just something i was  having some fun with  and then more and more people started  writing in to me and saying we want to  know more about your story we want to  know more about  what got you here and your advice and at  that time  everything was behind the scenes for me  i was always sharing stories of famous  entrepreneurs and their success and  showing examples but not too much about  my story  and i was shocked like why do people  care about my story  so i started sharing it more and more  you know my face wasn't even on the home  page  and so it got more and more me telling  my story and then i got invited to do  more speaking and  and then i started my youtube channel  and and social media and twitter and all  that stuff and it's it's built it's  built into this  amazing community right every video i  put up we get comments we get views and  get subscribers  i love it like the best part of my day  now is being  i wake up in the morning i grab my bowl  of lentils and i go to the computer and  look at the comments that i get from  youtube and my social media channels i  love that stuff  and it all came out of following  what i love doing having the courage to  not know where i'm going and just  explore things  and when i found something that i really  like to do even though it made no sense  to continue doing it  i continued on and found a way to turn  it into a business  and something that i'm still passionate  about i don't know 12 years later  11 years later 12 years still whatever  it doesn't matter still passionate about  it  so that's my story i don't know  hopefully that helps give you some  inspiration or helps answer your  question  let me know what you guys think you know  if you want more videos like this  leave a comment below let me know what  other questions you have i'm happy to do  a video  for you if you liked the video give it a  thumbs up  click on my face there subscribe to the  channel thank you so much  i'll see you soon

